(FOX40.COM) — A Woodland couple who are UC Davis employees are reported missing in Nepal and Tibet as flash flooding there has claimed over 1,000 victims, the Associated Press confirmed.

Hanumantha Rao Unnava, former dean of the UC Davis Graduate School of Management, and Vasu Unnava, an adjunct assistant professor at the university, had recently embarked on a retirement trip. Their plan was to go to Mount Kailash in Tibet before spending two months with family in India.

Hanumantha Rao Unnava (Credit: UC Davis)

The couple is now among dozens of United States citizens reported missing since the floods, which started in late August. Currently over 3,000 people have been reported missing as a result of the floods, the National Disaster Risk Reduction & Management Authority of Nepal reported.

